[E0440] Error: `tail` is `own<List>`, which cannot be cloned
    ╭─[ err/406_a_box_implements_nothing/main.wip:13:21 ]
    │
 11 │ @derive(Clone)
    │         ──┬──  
    │           ╰──── `@derive(Clone)` writes the clone field by field
    │ 
 13 │     Cons(head: i64, tail: own<List>)
    │                     ───────┬───────  
    │                            ╰───────── not a field that clones
    │ 
    │ Note: a field clones when its type implements `Clone`: plain data, which owns no memory, is its own clone, and so are a `String`, a `Vec`, an `Option` or a tuple of what clones, and a type that asks for `@derive(Clone)` or writes `extend …: Clone`
────╯
[E0342] Error: `own<Point>` does not implement `Eq`
    ╭─[ err/406_a_box_implements_nothing/main.wip:29:20 ]
    │
 22 │ fn same<T: Eq>(a: &T, b: &T): bool = a == b
    │         ┬  
    │         ╰── `T: Eq` declared here
    │ 
 29 │     io::println("\(same(&a, &b))")
    │                    ──────┬─────  
    │                          ╰─────── `T` requires `Eq`
    │ 
    │ Note: an `own<T>` implements nothing itself, whatever its `T` does; where `Point` is wanted, `&` of the box lends it, and a type argument written out, `<Point>`, asks for it
────╯
